    "id": "p30-q7-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "There are 11 buses available to transport 407 people on an outing. How many people will there be on each bus, if the passengers are to be distributed equally?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "37 people on each bus.",
      "worked": "Using short division, $40\\div11=3$ remainder $7$. Carry the $7$ tens to the ones column: $77\\div11=7$.\n\n$$407\\div11=37$$\n\nThere will be 37 people on each bus.",
